# Solver project. Every pattern below is relative to this file.
#
# The rule behind all of it: commit what cannot be regenerated, and commit the
# ledger that binds what is left out. Nothing here is a list that has to be
# edited when a new iteration starts -- that is what let iterations 36 and 37
# lose their frozen binaries under the previous version of this file.

# --- Build output --------------------------------------------------------
/build/
/build-*/
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
# (no bare CMakeCache.txt / CMakeFiles rule: /build*/ already covers local
# build trees, and a returned Kaggle run captures its own build output as
# evidence -- reports/kaggle-gpu-03/returned/ is a CUDA build log.)

# --- Local toolchains and reference builds -------------------------------
# Machine-local and large. Anything from them that mattered was frozen into
# reports/ at the time it was used.
/tools/local-toolchain/
/tools/reference/
/tools/data/emps.c

# --- Compiled binaries ---------------------------------------------------
# Ignored everywhere except under reports/, where the executable IS the
# evidence: each iteration's FINAL_STATE.json records its SHA-256, and the
# runtime DLLs beside it are what it was measured with. A pattern, so a new
# iteration needs no edit here.
*.exe
*.dll
!/reports/**/*.exe
!/reports/**/*.dll

# --- Model data ----------------------------------------------------------
# Public MIPLIB, Netlib and QPLIB instances are downloaded, not authored, and
# miplib2017-parta alone is 728 MiB. Every dataset folder keeps a manifest.json
# with the source URL and SHA-256 of each file (datasets/README.md), so the
# bytes are identified even when they are not stored.
#
# Declared holdout and fresh sets are the exception: the exact bytes an
# iteration measured on are part of that iteration's evidence.
/datasets/*/raw/
/datasets/*/*.mps
/datasets/*/*.qplib
/datasets/*/*.lp
/datasets/*/*.txt
!/datasets/*-holdout/*.mps
!/datasets/*-fresh/*.mps
!/datasets/*-guard*/*.mps

# --- Paired-run records --------------------------------------------------
# One solve writes <model>.<profile>[.<repeat>].json -- the captured monitor
# record, up to 31 MiB of solution vector and traces -- plus .ours.json and
# .reference.json beside it. Across iterations 30 to 37 that is ~3 GiB, with
# single files over GitHub's 50 MiB warning threshold.
#
# They stay on the machine that produced them, and the ledger that identifies
# them is committed: results.json in the same folder records every record's
# SHA-256, its model's SHA-256, the binary's SHA-256 and the exact command,
# and SUMMARY.json records results.json's own SHA-256. A two-dot name is a run
# record; every ledger, plan, profile and manifest has a single-dot name and is
# tracked.
/reports/**/*.*.json

# The validator outputs and captured streams that audit_*.py re-derive and
# assert against are NOT covered by that: archive_run_records.py packs them
# into checks.zip / streams.zip with a verified ARCHIVE.json, and those are
# committed.

# The command-line demonstration is a deliverable, not bulk: 875 KiB in total,
# and it is what the submission shows.
!/reports/demo-*/*.json

# Preserve files already tracked in the imported repository, even where its
# later ignore rules overlap them. See 10-project/repository/MIGRATION.md.
!/tools/reference/
!/tools/reference/**
!/build/
/build/*
!/build/emps.exe
!/build/solver_cli.exe
!/build/solver_tests.exe
